                            "steamid": "76561198037101281",
                            "num_reviews": 115,
                            "playtime_forever": 1705,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 601,
                            "last_played": 1756639578
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "These kinds of games have some mix of narative and sandbox. This one has a pretty even mix.\n\nSomething that this game does that most others don't is that it actually shows you the values you need in order to pull off most actions. This allows you to plan for future playthroughs if you like. \n\nWhat I love about the game is that there seem to be a ton of events that are specific to your actions in the game. If you went to college for a financial major, an opportunity for a ponsi scheme shows up later. If you get married and have a kid then you might find an event of the kid getting kidnapped. So many things happen that there is a lot of replay value.",
